WEBVTT

00:02:27.351 --> 00:02:30.151
We don't know for sure 
why this happens,

00:02:30.151 --> 00:02:32.910
but sometimes cues in the environment 
that remind us

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:37.060
of traumatic past experience 
can trigger a panic attack.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:39.688
Panic attacks can be part 
of anxiety disorders

00:02:39.688 --> 00:02:46.664
like PTSD, social anxiety disorder, OCD, 
and generalized anxiety disorder.

00:02:46.664 --> 00:02:50.374
Recurring panic attacks, 
frequent worry about new attacks,

00:02:50.374 --> 00:02:53.350
and behavioral changes 
to avoid panic attacks

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:57.120
can lead to a diagnosis 
of a panic disorder.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.522
The two main treatments 
for panic disorder

00:02:59.522 --> 00:03:05.374
are antidepressant medication 
and cognitive behavioral therapy, or CBT.